  "narrative": {
    "intro": "General Motors has $621M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Total award count across the available period is 13,654, with an average award size of $45.5K, and obligations are up 120.6% year over year. Obligations by fiscal year show a pattern of variation: FY21 $187M, FY22 $188M, FY23 $260M, FY24 $182M, FY25 $282M, and FY26 $621M. Current-year totals are partial, fiscal year to date. The figures reflect contract obligations except where tables list award-value figures as total contract values. These numbers show that FY26 obligations are a clear step above the prior years in absolute dollars and that GM handles a large volume of relatively small awards on average. Use the fiscal-year breakdown to spot timing shifts in obligations and to prioritize outreach or compliance work tied to peak obligation years. For procurement planning, focus on the high award count and the $45.5K average award size when sizing capture efforts and staffing for federal work.",
